WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:20.680
[MUSIC PLAYING]
[TURNTABLE SCRATCHING]

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:21.440
What up, y'all?

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:25.470
This is DJ Rob Swift, straight
from New York City, Queens,

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:28.860
here in the streets of
Cambridge, Massachusetts,

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.570
having fun at MIT.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:34.620
[TURNTABLE SCRATCHING]
MIT invited

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:39.420
me to teach a two week workshop
on six fundamental scratches.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:42.870
The foundation of all
scratch techniques.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:46.710
A lot of these techniques
took months, years to develop

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:49.110
and the students that
took this class were just

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.690
so excited and motivated
that they learned everything

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:52.290
in a day.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:53.950
And over the course
of the workshop,

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:57.500
they just practiced to
master the techniques.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:00.570
I myself, in general, have
just devoted my life's work

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:04.620
to teaching the art of DJing
to anyone that wants to learn.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.420
MIT being a progressive
school that it

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.540
has provided this
opportunity for me

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.690
to teach the students
here about DJing,

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:14.980
and not just the techniques
involved, you know,

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:17.940
moving a record back and forth,
but the culture and the history

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:20.110
behind it.

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:22.840
You can go on YouTube and watch
a quick five minute tutorial

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:27.460
but not have context on how rich
the history is behind this art

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:28.830
form.

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:32.490
And I'm just super
grateful and glad that we

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:35.430
get to bring something
like this to MIT.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:38.180
[TURNTABLE SCRATCHING]

